          "text": "# RFC 001: Extensible Architecture - Key Concepts\n\n## Main File Types/Categories\n\nThe proposal organizes configuration into distinct YAML files within a specifications directory:\n\n1. **SLO Specifications** - User-defined service level objectives (e.g., `platform/reliable_service.yaml`)\n2. **Basic Types** - Attribute definitions with their data types\n3. **SLI Types** - Service Level Indicator type definitions with query templates\n4. **Services** - Service definitions listing supported SLI types\n\n## Specification vs. Instantiation\n\n**Specifications** are templates or type definitions that establish structure and rules. For example, an SLI type specification defines query template variables like `graphql_operation_name` and `environment`.\n\n**Instantiations** are concrete implementations using those specifications. An SLO instantiation fills in actual values: `graphql_operation_name: \"createappointment\"` and `environment: \"production\"`.\n\n## Specification Types Mentioned\n\n1. **BasicType** - Individual typed attributes with names and accepted data types\n2. **QueryTemplateType** - Templates containing parameterized queries with variable specifications\n3. **SliType** - Complete SLI definitions combining query templates, variable specifications, and instantiated queries\n4. **Service** - Collections of supported SLI types available to services",
